Live-draw keeps two frames in flight: the present flush waits for frame N-1, not the frame it just submitted.

Each frame slot has its own command allocator, upload/vertex/index/vertex-constant/pixel-constant rings,
shader-visible SRV and sampler heaps, and retired-texture list. The present flush (LD_FLUSH_PRESENT) closes and
queues frame N, waits for the other slot's fence (frame N-1), releases that slot's retired textures, switches the
ring pointers to it and resets the ring cursors. Every other flush (rings full, guest reference, readback, movie,
shutdown) stays synchronous and keeps the current slot. The movie path's offset-0 upload write waits for idle first.
LD_FRAMES_IN_FLIGHT=1 restores the old model. LD_NO_PRESENT=1 (diagnostic) skips the swap-chain Present so
RSX_PERF shows the renderer's own throughput without the display path.

